    "q-35222": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35222",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the vector $x$, if $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]= \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
