    "q-112246": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112246",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-14 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=8.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(8)=-14\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-6)+8=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
