    "q-112254": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112254",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom third equation we get ${x}_{3}=-1$ and substituting this value into the second equation yields ${x}_{2}=-2(-1)+3=5.$ Finally, substituting ${x}_{2}=5$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(5)+2(-1)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=(-6)+5+(-1)=-2.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
